<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Just the "F" (ic_forvia_logo_vector.xml's ink1/ink2 paths, no side bars) — Android 12+'s own
  SplashScreen API (windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon, values-v31/styles.xml) masks whatever it's
  given into a square/circular icon slot, and the full wide bars+F lockup doesn't fit that shape
  without looking clipped. This is what plays in THAT system-owned slot, briefly, before
  SplashActivity's own layout (the real, full animation) takes over.
-->
